===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|pt|-}}, named after {{w|Saint Paul}}. {{doublet|en|Saint Paul}}. The city was originally named "São Paulo dos Campos de Piratininga" meaning "Saint Paul of the fields of Piratininga". "Piratininga" comes from {{der|en|tpw|pirá||fish}} and {{der|en|tpw|tininga||to dry}} meaning "dried fish", after the fish that would be stranded on the shore of the {{w|Tietê River}} after a flood and left to dry out.

